er bound \\(|\\mathcal T|\\ge 2n-2\\).  \nFrom (2) we have an explicit tiling achieving \\(|\\mathcal T|=2n-2\\).  \nHence the bound is tight, and the minimum possible number of tiles equals \\(2n-2\\).\n\nFor the concrete size \\(n=2025\\),\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\cdot2025-2=4048}\n\\]\n\ntiles are necessary and sufficient.  \n\nThe explicit construction described above (with the main diagonal left uncovered and the \\(2024\\) “upper’’ and \\(2024\\) “lower’’ rectangles) provides the required example."
